# Soma Messages' own notifications (0.7+), linked to the Mac service's DEMO on the Mac Pro (sample chats only; every
# send gets a fake reply 2 s later). A message that arrives while the app is in the background notifies; Reply in the
# shade sends; tapping opens the conversation.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
key HOME
shell pm clear dev.omalauncher.messages
shell pm grant dev.omalauncher.messages android.permission.READ_CONTACTS
shell pm grant dev.omalauncher.messages android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS
shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d "'soma-messages://link?url=http%3A%2F%2F100.120.219.46%3A8765&token=BON7avwraojOZCR1WT8sLWZg9WTx0RFaqeR3udg1kzA'" dev.omalauncher.messages
wait 2500
tap Link
wait 4000
expect Ana Demo
# Linked: the quiet notice that keeps it in touch with the Mac.
shell cmd statusbar expand-notifications
wait 1200
expect Connected to your Mac
shot link-notice
shell cmd statusbar collapse
wait 800
tap Ana Demo
wait 2000
tap 0.5 0.925
wait 600
type notify test
wait 400
key ENTER
# Away before the demo's answer (2 s): it arrives in the background.
key HOME
wait 4000
shell cmd statusbar expand-notifications
wait 1500
expect Demo reply to: notify test
expect Reply
expect Mark read
shot message-notification
tap Demo reply to: notify test
wait 2500
# The tap opens the conversation, and its notification goes.
expect Perfect, see you there
expect Demo reply to: notify test
shot opened-from-notification
shell cmd statusbar expand-notifications
wait 1200
absent Demo reply to: notify test
shell cmd statusbar collapse
[phone] Real service: lock the Fold, have someone text Boss: one notification, with the name from contacts, sound as Android sets it; Reply from the lock screen goes out from his number.
[phone] After a restart of the Fold, "Connected to your Mac" is back without opening the app.
[phone] OpenBubbles' own notifications: Boss decides whether to turn them off, so each message doesn't notify twice.
